 "title": "Nutritional Strategies and Disease Resistance in Aquatic Organisms",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on nutritional strategies and disease resistance in aquatic organisms. Taurine, a chemical, has favorable responses in several fish species, including European seabass, Gilthead seabream, Olive flounder, and Red seabream. Probiotics and hydrolysates are used for nutritional-balancing strategies, which require advanced validation and disease resistance. Vibrio parahaemolyticus, a pathogenic organism, is a challenge for disease resistance in Olive flounder and Whiteleg shrimp. The cluster also includes various fishmeal and fermented ingredients, as well as chemicals like DHA and EPA, which are likely used in nutritional-balancing strategies.",
